# Paths the handbook checks skip, one per line: a glob, or `kind: glob`.
# A bare glob skips the path in every check; `orphan:` exempts it from the
# orphan check alone, and `em-dash:` from the em dash check alone. A trailing /
# covers everything below, and * spans directory separators. Write the reason
# beside each line, and delete what does not apply here.
# Handbook: /handbook/meta/local/README.md says what this repository does not
# author, and the shared rules say what needs no backreference; both belong
# here, by kind.

# Vendored skills and commands are nobody's to reformat.
em-dash: .claude/

# The vendored C library is upstream's, and the Stimulus subrepo is its own
# project; what this repository changes about either is patch/ and
# tools/stimulus/ (handbook/architecture/engine/, architecture/stimulus/).
src/vendor/cigraph/
tools/py-stimulus/

# Generated documents cannot carry a backreference; the generator does.
# NEWS.md is fledge's, the snapshots testthat's, and revdep/ holds reports
# revdepcheck writes and the notes kept beside them for one release.
NEWS.md
orphan: tests/testthat/_snaps/
revdep/

# Generated sources carry the generator's header line, punctuation included
# (handbook/architecture/stimulus/).
em-dash: R/aaa-*.R

# The rendered README comes from README.Rmd and is read from a tarball that
# does not carry handbook/, so its pointer is the site rather than a link the
# checks can resolve (handbook/meta/local/).
orphan: README.md

# The submission comments reach a CRAN maintainer verbatim, so they link to
# nothing internal; handbook/operations/releases/ links to them.
orphan: cran-comments.md
orphan: cran-comments.template.md

# The series tooling keeps duckdb-r's punctuation so that a resync stays a
# clean diff (.series-source); the rest of these paths predate the rule, and
# handbook/meta/local/ exempts them rather than rewriting them.
em-dash: scripts/
em-dash: tools/
em-dash: CONTRIBUTING.md

# The list of the C library's authors, kept beside the package for reference:
# data, not prose, and it needs no route into the tree.
orphan: AUTHORS-list.md
